We would like to clarify an issue regarding the upload history of our project repository.
In our submission records, there are timeout upload logs. This occurred because after programming the bitfile onto the NetFPGA board, we were unable to ping between 2 nodes. 
To diagnose the issue, we sought guidance from senior students who had previously taken the course. After reviewing our code, they confirmed that there were no obvious logical errors. 
To further isolate the problem and rule out potential hardware issues, they attempted to run their own project files on the board.
However, during the subsequent GitHub upload process, both project folders had identical names. As a result, we mistakenly uploaded their project files instead of our own.
While reviewing our Lab4 implementation during Lab5, we discovered this mistake and immediately re-uploaded our correct project files.
We sincerely apologize for any confusion or inconvenience this may have caused and respectfully ask for your understanding. Thank you.
